			"Message": "feat(Element): Sync submodule updates delivering Workbench service layers\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n- Wind (b91de584): Add WorkbenchClipboard, WorkbenchHost, and WorkbenchKeybinding services. Three new Effect-TS service layers bridging VS Code's native workbench services: WorkbenchClipboardService (read/write text and resources), WorkbenchHostService (reload, restart, close, focus operations), and WorkbenchKeybindingService (keybinding lookup and resolution). Each follows the established Wind pattern with Context.Tag, interface, Live implementation, and Problem ADT.\n- Output, Worker: Submodule pointer updates with internal improvements.\n- Rest, SideCar, Sky: Submodule pointer updates.\n\nThis synchronization delivers the final tier of Wind workbench services, completing the service layer coverage for VS Code integration.",
			"SHA": "77871c6b08f9673b272bb742f3844946326a5b65"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T04:59:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add Workbench* Effect-TS service layers\n\nAdd six new workbench-tier service layers bridging VS Code's native workbench services to Wind's Effect-TS architecture:\n- WorkbenchCommandService: Execute/list/filter commands, stream command execution events\n- WorkbenchDialogService: Confirm dialogs, pick choices, show info/warn/error\n- WorkbenchLifecycleService: Phase tracking (Starting/Ready/Restored/Eventually), shutdown streams\n- WorkbenchNotificationService: Dispatch notifications, stream dispatched events\n- WorkbenchStorageService: Scope-aware (Application/Profile/Workspace) storage with targets\n- WorkbenchThemeService: Get/set color themes, token color queries, theme change streams\n\nEach service provides a typed Effect-TS interface with Live implementation (runtime bridge via globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__) and Problem ADT for error handling, following the established pattern in Wind of exposing Context.Tag, interface, and Layer for dependency injection.\n\nRefs: Land/.claude/tauri/Patches/14-StreamingGRPC.md",
			"SHA": "5ca5ec8c8bb81e041398e9cece2a621d23b4aadb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T04:54:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates delivering WKWebView font fixes and service layers\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n- Mountain (27cc378d): Add explicit font MIME type mappings for WKWebView. Add TTF, OTF, WOFF, WOFF2, EOT mappings to resolve silent font loading failures where codicon font and extension assets (KaTeX, Seti) render as blank squares.\n- Output (b20d23f9): Expand workbench service exposure with 21 new handles (Configuration, Storage, Lifecycle, Theme, etc.) for Wind consumption. Add InjectConfigurationOverlay and InjectStorageOverlay transforms for runtime config/storage overrides via globalThis.__CEL_OVERRIDE_CONFIG__ and __CEL_OVERRIDE_STORAGE__. Also fix worker URL rewriting and CSS loader handling.\n- Wind (b0f1a825): Add UserSettings and WorkbenchStorage Effect-TS services. UserSettingsService bridges VS Code's IConfigurationService with memory target support; WorkbenchStorageService provides scope-aware storage with change streams.\n- Cocoon, Mountain, Output, Wind: Submodule pointer updates.",
			"SHA": "94a05df58bbdaad74254673d7504bc0d6a48ce87"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T03:49:11Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠃⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				7
			],
			"Message": "build(Element): Sync submodule updates with ESBuild config refactor and minification\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n- Output: Switch from esbuild transform to byte-copy for VS Code sources. Change VSCode.ts ESBuild config to use `loader: { \".js\": \"copy\" }` instead of parsing/transforming VS Code's out/ tree. This byte-copies .js/.cjs/.mjs files directly, preserving tsc's original identifiers and fixing transform plugins that were silently no-oping due to esbuild's minification.\n- Wind: Minify ESBuild configuration and Target output files. Compress configuration from multi-line readable format to single-line minified output, rebuild Target/ with reduced file sizes.\n- Worker: Minify ESBuild configuration files. Replace descriptive variable names with single letters, remove whitespace and comments.\n- Mountain, Cocoon, Common, Maintain: Submodule pointer updates.\n\nThis synchronization fixes the Output transform pipeline while reducing bundle sizes through minification across Wind and Worker.",
			"SHA": "c969a037ce0f0f7f812d7619f2779764bab99468"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T02:27:58Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
